3     Structural Optimal Jacobian Accumulation is NP-complete
In this section, we show that Structural Optimal Jacobian Accumulation is NP-complete.
We reduce from Vertex Cover, which is defined as follows.

    Vertex Cover
    Input:           An undirected graph G = (V, E) and an integer k.
    Question:        Is there a set C ⊆ V of at most k vertices such that each edge in E has at
                     least one endpoint in C?


Theorem 1. Structural Optimal Jacobian Accumulation is NP-complete. Assuming the
ETH, it cannot be solved in 2o(n+m) time.

