6    Conclusion
We have resolved a pair of longstanding open questions by showing that Structural Optimal
Jacobian Accumulation and Minimum Edge Count are both NP-complete. Our progress opens
the door to many interesting questions. On the theoretical side, a key next step is to understand the
complexities of both problems under the more expressive edge elimination operation [18]. There are
also promising opportunities to develop approximation algorithms and/or establish lower bounds.


