The Track B construction passed local G1–G8 checks, including 0/200,000 random guesses and five attacks at 0/8. However, the oracle pool solved every level through the escalation cap, including `n=420`, producing the required `too_easy` verdict.

I documented the analysis and exact results in [REJECTED.md](/Users/jang-wongi/Desktop/WG/PI_LAB/arxiv-gv-problems/results/2506.17521/REJECTED.md). The harness evidence is preserved in [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/Users/jang-wongi/Desktop/WG/PI_LAB/arxiv-gv-problems/results/2506.17521/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl) and [.meta.json](/Users/jang-wongi/Desktop/WG/PI_LAB/arxiv-gv-problems/results/2506.17521/.meta.json).

The draft [generator module](/Users/jang-wongi/Desktop/WG/PI_LAB/arxiv-gv-problems/results/2506.17521/gen_2506_17521.py) remains solely as reproducible rejection evidence. Per the task rules, I did not retune past the verdict or manufacture G9/shipping deliverables.
